Fix OUTPUT DQBUF: buffer queue management, blocking/non-blocking behaviour
and STREAMOFF wakeup.

VIDIOC_DQBUF on the OUTPUT side returned buffers that were never queued via
VIDIOC_QBUF, which GStreamer v4l2sink reports as "buffer X was not queued,
this indicate a driver bug" (e.g. icamerasrc ! v4l2sink in v4l2-relayd).
DQBUF now returns only queued buffers, honours O_NONBLOCK (-EAGAIN) or
blocks otherwise, and is woken up by STREAMOFF.

Backport of the following commits onto v0.15.4, squashed:
  2f8f35e Fix buffer queue management to comply with V4L2 specification
  345ca04 Fix OUTPUT DQBUF O_NONBLOCK and blocking behaviour
  6ba4512 Wake blocked OUTPUT DQBUF on STREAMOFF
  0baebb6 Preserve bufpos2index mapping in prepare_buffer_queue()

Upstream: https://github.com/v4l2loopback/v4l2loopback/pull/656
Bug: https://github.com/v4l2loopback/v4l2loopback/issues/383
Signed-off-by: Shih-Yuan Lee (FourDollars) <sylee@canonical.com>

